### MS3 Demanda - testes com login pelo MS4 (extensao "REST Client").
### Rode na ordem. Ajuste as portas conforme o .env de cada servico.
### IMPORTANTE: o JWT_SECRET do MS3 tem que ser IGUAL ao do MS4.

@ms4 = http://localhost:7505
@ms3 = http://localhost:7504

### 1) Login de um ADMIN no MS4 (usar o ADMIN real)
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{ms4}}/auth/login/admin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@hemovida.com", "senha": "hemoLBR*&senac" }

### 2) Criar um GESTOR_DEMANDA no MS4.
### hospitalId = o hospital_id de um hospital que JA EXISTE na tabela hospital do MS3 (ativo).
POST {{ms4}}/usuarios
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.access_token}}

{
  "perfil": "GESTOR_DEMANDA",
  "nomeCompleto": "Gestor Paulo Teste",
  "email": "gestor.paulo.teste@hemovida.com",
  "senha": "paulo54321",
  "hospitalId": 1
}

### 3) Login do gestor no MS4 (devolve o token que o MS3 aceita)
# @name loginGestor
POST {{ms4}}/auth/login/admin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "gestor.paulo.teste@hemovida.com", "senha": "paulo54321" }

### 4) MS3 sem token (deve dar 401)
GET {{ms3}}/requests

### 5) Criar pedido (201)
POST {{ms3}}/requests
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginGestor.response.body.access_token}}

{
  "tipo": "REPOSICAO",
  "itens": [
    { "tipoSanguineo": "O-", "hemocomponente": "PLAQUETAS", "quantidadeBolsas": 3 }
  ]
}

### 6) Listar pedidos do meu hospital (200)
GET {{ms3}}/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{loginGestor.response.body.access_token}}

### 7) Buscar um pedido (troque o 1 pelo id que apareceu)
GET {{ms3}}/requests/7
Authorization: Bearer {{loginGestor.response.body.access_token}}

### 8) Cancelar (200 se estava PENDENTE)
PATCH {{ms3}}/requests/8/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{loginGestor.response.body.access_token}}

### 9) Token do ADMIN no MS3 (deve dar 403: so GESTOR_DEMANDA acessa)
GET {{ms3}}/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.access_token}}
